      "title": "READ ME · existing Krea 2 → 16-bit anchor → LTX → final-frame loop",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# SineForge · Krea 2 + LTX-2.3 Lossless Continuation Loop\n\n1. Load any starting image.\n2. Load an Ingredients/reference sheet in node 1B. Use a clean panel sheet for recurring characters, wardrobe, props, style, or studio/set identity.\n3. Set `loop_count` on node 2. Values 1+ run exactly that many cycles. Set 0 to keep going until you press ComfyUI Interrupt.\n4. On node 3, describe any `scene_or_subject` and the `next_event`. The defaults make no assumption about people, podcasts, or dialogue.\n5. Choose `audio_mode`: automatic from scene, no dialogue, dialogue JSON, or advanced JSON only. `dialogue_json` is optional and defaults to `[]`.\n6. For exact speech, choose dialogue JSON and use entries such as `[{\"speaker\":\"Character A\",\"position\":\"camera-left\",\"line\":\"Exact words\"}]`.\n7. Keep `recent_cycles_json` as `[]` unless you paste valid JSON history. The advanced `continuation_request_json` remains available for full-contract control.\n8. Node 3 lists every local executable GGUF package. Qwen 3.6 40B is the default only. Vision models see both images; text-only models receive the JSON scene request without image attachments. Krea still uses both images through `Krea2EncodeRebalance`.\n9. The LTX model path uses the official Ingredients IC-LoRA plus LTX reference-token conditioning, then feeds the patched model into the Sulphur all-in-one node via `model_override`.\n10. The Krea sampler creates a fresh 768×448 anchor. Node 14 saves it as 16-bit PNG and passes the same unmodified tensor into LTX.\n11. LTX produces native audio/video. Node 16 saves a lossless FFV1 + FLAC master.\n12. Node 18 extracts the true final tensor frame before encoding. Node 20 saves it as 16-bit PNG and passes the same tensor into the next cycle.\n13. Every planner artifact and all editable dialogue are JSON. No hosted/API agent is used.\n\n**Lossless scope:** PNG/FFV1/FLAC storage and in-memory handoffs avoid additional codec loss. Krea and LTX generation themselves are generative and cannot be mathematically lossless."
      ],
      "color": "#26354f",
      "bgcolor": "#172237"
    }
